WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.240
Get out your paddles.

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:03.240
"Ooh, you better believe that's a paddlin'."

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:08.760
And celebrate Jingles Day, because this 
episode has more twists than a f*cking roller coaster.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:16.360
Yes, episode 3 of "American Horror Story: 1984"
is jam-packed with cool kills and new theories,

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.900
so I'm gonna break down the episode
and what it could mean for the season.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.720
You'll want to stick
around till the very end

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:26.920
for even more tinfoil hat conspiracies about
Montana, Brooke, and the Night Stalker.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:28.920
So here we go.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:34.460
The episode begins right where we left off with the Night Stalker trying to break down the door to the infirmary.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.480
We saw him last episode nearing
his way to Ray, Chet, Brooke and Rita,

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.960
who have gone in search of the car
keys so they can make their escape.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.080
The Night Stalker smashes his way through
the window, which they quickly board up,

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.840
when Ray has quite possibly
the stupidest suggestion ever:

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.680
The four of them split up and the
slowest will be the one who gets caught.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.240
"That's ... that's stupid."

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:02.200
But before a plan can be made, the Night Stalker
bursts through the door and Ray gets caught in his way.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.540
Now here is where I caught
something really weird.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:09.500
This is the shot of Ray right when
the Night Stalker bursts down the door.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.360
Take note of his jacket.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.400
We then cut to the Night
Stalker and then back to Ray,

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.880
but look at his jacket now:
covered in blood splatter.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:22.040
Now, this could a) just be a simple
mistake they made when filming,

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.100
or b) if you believe the
theory that they're all actors

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:29.440
or that this is some sort of Groundhog
Day that repeats over and over again,

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.520
it could be another subtle hint
that that's what we're watching.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:37.880
Ray gets the crap slashed out of him and is saved
by Chet, who rams the Night Stalker into the window.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:40.580
And instead of finishing him off,
they just kind of leave him there.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:45.640
Meanwhile at the other camp, Montana and
Trevor try to snap Xavier out of his shell shock,

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.920
while they believe Mr. Jingles
is trying to make his way in.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:55.000
Now, there's something interesting here, too. Right before Jingles leaves, there's a sound of a motorcycle.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:02.300
But we can't be sure if this is from
the two pranksters or someone else.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.920
The pranksters hurl
a flaming bag of crap

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:09.080
But here's yet another weird editing,
and I'm hesitant to say it, mistake.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:13.280
Check out this shot of the flaming poo
taken from the season to come preview

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.200
and compare it to the one
that was shown this episode.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:19.480
One is clearly wearing a
mask, while the other is not.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:24.240
Is this just a mistake and they
reshot it or digitally added in a mask?

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.620
Who knows, but these little
mistakes are starting to add up.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:33.120
The fun is short-lived as the two pranksters
are viciously murdered by the real Mr. Jingles.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.760
Apparently, it's customary for local
kids to play pranks during "Jingles Day",

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:40.460
the anniversary of the
Camp Redwood massacre.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:45.760
Jingles cuts off one of the kid's ears as
Trevor, Montana, and Xavier make a run for it.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:51.700
Brooke and Rita have split from Chet and Ray when we hear a scream coming from Chet and Ray's direction.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.140
They've fallen into a pit of spikes and Chet
seems to have gotten the worst of the two.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.340
Now, what's interesting about this is that it
couldn't have been Jingles who set up this trap.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:03.740
He just got to Camp
Redwood a few hours ago,

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:07.100
so someone else must have
riddled these woods with traps.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:11.860
My best guess is that this was Rita, as we'll
later find out she's in cahoots with Jingles.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.560
Now this is another interesting scene.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.780
Jingle stumbles across one of the pranksters

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:20.640
who we learn was brought in to the
prank because his mother paid the other kids.

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:27.360
He doesn't have glasses, uses an inhaler, has reverence for Jingles, and just wants to be a badass for the night.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:29.120
Jingles lets him live.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:34.640
Now, it could be because Jingles feels
sorry for him or sees a bit of himself in this kid.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:38.240
Either way, it proves that there's
more to Jingles than meets the eye.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:41.380
He doesn't simply kill
everything that gets in his way.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:46.700
Ray tries to get the spike out of Chet's shoulder,
but if he does, Chet will likely bleed to death.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:50.120
Chet thinks it was Jingles who
dug the pit since it's a punji pit,

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:53.400
a trap used by the Viet Cong
during the Vietnam War.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.620
And we know Jingles used to fight Nam.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:00.880
But if Rita is working with Jingles, it's possible that
she could have learned about these traps through him.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.980
Brooke and Rita are waiting for the others
when Brooke suggests they go and get help.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.040
Rita says,

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:10.560
"And leave everyone here to fend for themselves?
Your friends wouldn't bail on you like that."

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:12.240
Uh, we know one who would.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:17.480
Rita gives her the keys, and in the first big twist of
the season, she drugs Brooke before she can go,

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:20.940
showing us that she's in league with
Jingles, which we'll get into in a bit.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:26.380
After all, last episode, we saw her confronted
by him, but we never saw the actual fight.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.960
They were likely planning out the next steps.

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:33.380
We find out a week ago that Rita is actually
renowned psychologist Donna Chambers.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:39.720
So good, in fact, she was able to get new information out of such killers as Ted Bundy and John Wayne Gacy.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:43.480
Also interesting to note that John
Carroll Lynch, the man who plays Jingles,

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:46.440
also played Gacy in
season seven's "Cult".

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:51.000
Whereas Hopple believes some people are
simply pure evil, Donna believes otherwise,

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.960
and is able to convince
Hopple of letting her interview him.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.860
Donna meets with Jingles and
is able to break through to him.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:01.980
Everyone has said he's an irredeemable
monster, but Donna believes otherwise.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:05.980
External events, such as
Vietnam, caused him to go crazy.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:11.720
If she can pinpoint what made him snap in what he did, she can maybe prevent future killings from happening.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:16.920
We also learn that Jingles never remembered
killing those kids. That's very important.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:20.540
And it was actually the doctors
who said he had this psychotic break,

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:25.140
leaving the theory that it was
Margaret who's the real killer still on the table.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:28.300
Rita's talk about trauma
being a cause for serial killing

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:34.140
could also correlate with characters like Brooke and Xavier, who have had traumatic experiences in the past.

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:37.220
Donna proposes an
absolutely outrageous plan:

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:40.060
She needs to witness
Jingles in his natural habitat,

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:43.820
and helps him break out by
providing him with his bag and knife.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.920
But when Jingles prods her as to
why'd she do this, she simply says,

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:49.700
"I have my reasons."

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:54.320
So don't count out that Donna has an
ulterior motive for this entire operation.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:59.420
And here we have our first glimpse of the real
nurse Rita, who we saw in the preview video.

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:05.060
Donna is following her as they drive into
Roy's gas station, the same one from episode 1.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:10.160
Rita suggests they convoy up and
Donna says something very peculiar here.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:15.040
"If you ask me, all those murders are
because of the availability of pornography,

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.540
and the objectification
of women in our culture."

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:21.440
This is the second time she's
mentioned how bad pornography is,

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:24.160
and I can't help but
think how in episode 1,

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:27.720
Margaret ranted about how she
fought alongside Charles Keating,

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:30.580
an anti-pornographer
who took on Larry Flynt.

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:35.320
It makes me wonder if there is a deeper
connection between Margaret and Donna.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:38.820
And this is exactly what I'd expect a
gas-station washroom to look like.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:42.680
Rita returns to find Donna missing, so
she heads on over to Camp Redwood

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:45.040
only to find Rita in the back of her car.

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:48.540
We flash forward to find that
Rita isn't really a nurse - shocker -

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:51.300
and that she gave
Brooke horse tranquilizers.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:55.680
Speaking of people passed out, we have
Chet, who doesn't seem to be doing too well.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:59.780
Ray thinks this is the perfect
opportunity to get something off his chest,

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:02.320
so he tells him his
traumatic experience.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:05.300
Remember that trauma has
been a big part of this season.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:09.300
But how the writers are gonna wrap it
all together thematically remains to be seen.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:11.980
We learn that Ray left
L.A. because he was in trouble.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:18.120
During a hazing incident for his fraternity,
Omega Xi, a new recruit, Chan, falls down the stairs

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.760
and Ray believes he's dead.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.960
Instead of calling an ambulance and
jeopardizing the future of the fraternity,

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:27.480
Ray takes one for the team
and throws Chan off a cliff.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.980
But Chan isn't dead.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:32.060
Ray tries to help him,
but Chan rips off his watch.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:36.520
When Ray found out Chan's car had been
found and his watch would be inside the car,

00:07:36.520 --> 00:07:38.320
he knew he had
to get out of the city.

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:42.120
This incident made Ray drop out
of school and get a job at a hospital.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:45.100
We learned in episode 1
that Ray used to be an orderly,

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:48.620
so it's possible he could have a
connection to Jingles' asylum.

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:54.380
Ray learns that Chet heard his entire story and decides to leave the guy who, moments ago, saved his life.

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:56.740
This is not a great
look for Ray this episode.

00:07:56.740 --> 00:08:01.460
Trevor, Montana, and Xavier argue
about saving Margaret and Bertie. After all,

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.560
"Chef Bertie is good people."

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:05.400
Hiding in the
boathouse, they find Rita.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:11.060
Remember, it was Donna who drugged her, not
Jingles, so we can deduce that Donna isn't a murderer.

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:15.520
She's merely setting up things for Jingles to
finish off later, which is exactly what he does.

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:20.160
Again, I could totally be looking too deep into
things, but my eyes were drawn to this locket.

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:25.680
And I'm wondering if it were to be opened, if there would be a picture of her and any of the other characters.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:30.640
Ray runs into Xavier, Trevor, and Montana
and lies to them about how he lost Chet.

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:36.380
They tell him that Rita isn't the real Rita, and Ray argues with them about going back to save Margaret and Bertie.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:41.500
Trevor gives him his motorcycle keys and
tells him to go to the call box to call the police.

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:44.573
But now that we know Ray
is likely wanted by the police

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:47.680
and earlier this episode
said every man for himself,

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:50.440
My guess is that he'd
never call the police, anyway.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.140
Montana goes with Ray as well,

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:57.240
and this also makes sense because earlier, she argued against going back to look for Margaret and Bertie.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.460
Jingles is alerted to the
sound of Chet, but it's a fake out.

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:04.920
Xavier and Trevor help him out, and they
learn the truth: that Ray left Chet to die.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:09.480
Trevor musters his Big Dick Energy and
throws who he thinks is Jingles into the pit.

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:13.140
But it's actually our inhaler guy
we met earlier in the episode.

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:18.880
But what I think is most interesting is the absence of
this shot, which we saw in the season to come trailer.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:22.160
We have Jingles pouring
gasoline into the pit with Ray.

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:27.020
Now this could mean a few things: a) that
this is something we'll see in the future,

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:30.100
b) it's a total fake out
just to throw us off,

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:35.760
but usually, a show wouldn't go through the lengths of shooting this just for a quick 1-second shot in the trailer.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:39.760
Or c) that we're going to eventually
deal with multiple timelines,

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:43.840
that we'll come back to Camp Redwood somehow
and the characters will go through the same night

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:45.460
but different things will happen.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.760
Ray and Montana make
a run for the parking lot,

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:53.460
but as soon as they're confronted by the Night Stalker, Ray takes the motorcycle, leaving Montana in the dust.

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:57.600
But he finally gets what's coming to
him as Mr. Jingles decapitates him.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:03.060
But before he dies, Ray says what I think is
the most important line in the entire episode:

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:06.900
Quote: "Suck a nut, Camp
Redwood. See you in another life."

00:10:06.900 --> 00:10:10.780
Now we've already seen one character
have multiple lives: the hitchhiker.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:15.140
And we previously discussed this
shot of Ray in the pit with Mr. Jingles.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:19.980
Is it possible this night repeats over and
over like some sort of Groundhog Day?

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:23.140
The end of the episode leaves
us with another huge twist:

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:26.000
that Montana and the
Night Stalker are lovers,

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:29.900
ending with Montana asking
why he hasn't "killed her yet".

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:32.520
This "her" is likely
referring to Brooke.

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:36.020
After all, we already know the
Night Stalker and Brooke have a history.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:41.900
But the history we've seen is from Brooke's
perspective. What if that perspective isn't reliable?

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:46.260
From this brief interaction, it seems
Montana is the one pulling the strings.

00:10:46.420 --> 00:10:48.880
She's the one with the
vendetta against Brooke.

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:52.540
What if there's a more nefarious
side to Brooke we haven't seen?

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:56.300
One of the more curious shots we
saw this season was in episode 1

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.900
where Brooke briefly
shows us her jewelry box.

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:01.180
Not only are there a few rings here,

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:06.380
but later that night when the Night Stalker visits
her, the first thing he asked for is her jewelry.

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:13.080
The Night Stalker came into her house with the intention of finding this specific ring at the behest of Montana,

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:17.420
which is the same exact ring we see
in the wedding flashback in episode 2.

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:22.940
This likely means there is some sort of connection between Montana, the ring, and Joseph Cavanaugh.

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:27.820
Perhaps Montana was a jealous ex-lover
or a family member hell-bent on revenge.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:29.940
We'll need to stay tuned to find out.

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:34.420
This episode was nuts, and as always, I want
to hear your theories in the comments below.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:37.440
Make sure to give the video a
like and subscribe with the bell on

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:40.200
to get the latest "American
Horror Story" breakdowns.

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:43.240
You can also find me on
Twitter @ThinkStoryYT.

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:44.740
Until next time remember,

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:46.380
Daddy loves you very much.

